    "reading": {
        "body": "Embedding models dominate actual Hugging Face usage: the single most-downloaded model, sentence-transformers/all-MiniLM-L6-v2, accounts for roughly 253 million downloads against a daily total near two billion, making it far more widely pulled than any generative model in the top twelve.\n\nThe download series shows a step change between August 20 and August 22, where daily totals jumped from around 1.54 billion to roughly 1.98 billion and held there. What caused that shift is not in the data. What the data does show is that once the new level was established it was stable, which suggests a persistent change in demand rather than a spike from a single event. At two billion daily downloads across 16,369 tracked models, the inference and fine-tuning workloads implied are substantial, though the data does not map downloads to compute hours or power consumption.\n\nThe licence distribution is worth noting for anyone reasoning about commercial deployment. Apache-2.0 covers 7,081 of the 16,369 models, more than all other declared licences combined. MIT adds another 2,301. Together those two permissive licences account for the majority of the catalogue. However, 1,860 models carry no declared licence, and 1,683 fall under a catch-all \"other\" category, meaning roughly a fifth of the models tracked here have ambiguous or non-standard terms. The data covers licence counts only, not download volumes by licence, so the commercial risk concentration cannot be read directly from these numbers.",
